40,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, the numbers are in! It looks like a couple of people are practically living in that room while the rest of us barely visit. And as for the crumbs... yikes. Someone's been snacking!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"It seems the mess isn't just in the break room. I found that several desks in the office have crumbs too, and the bins are being emptied daily. People are eating at their workstations.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Servas,,It is revealing that we have spent a significant amount on outside rentals for very small groups. We must ask ourselves if we are creating obstacles for ourselves that a simple internal solution could solve.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Whoa, Servas is right! We've spent 68,000 yen just to go somewhere else! That's a lot of ice cream money! And the new stuff costs 141,000 or 96,000 yen. Which one should we pick?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wait, the money is one thing, but did you guys hear? We're barely talking! The only unplanned chats are by the printer, and the last awkward talk happened right in front of everyone. We really need a private spot!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, a private spot sounds lovely, but if only two people are actually using the room, is it really a ""shared"" space? It feels more like a private club for the people by the door!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, it's not about a private club. The issue is that the current wall is just plasterboard; you can hear everything inside from the desks. If we want privacy, we need a real solution.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Servas,,"We must be careful not to let our desire for privacy create a new burden of maintenance. If we build walls, who will tend to the space? Let us seek a path of least resistance.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"But we can all help clean up! If we have a cool room, it'll be way more fun to keep it tidy. @Misaki, if the wall is too thin, maybe the screen and table fit-out would help us use it better?","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, exactly! If we have a place where we can actually talk without everyone listening, we'll want to be there more. We can't just be strangers who only chat by the printer!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, I love the enthusiasm, but let's be real: if we just make it ""private,"" the same two people will just hog it more. We need a system for who gets to be in there!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a system won't fix the sound leakage. Even if we rotate users, the people sitting nearby will still hear every word. We need to address the physical environment first if we want actual privacy.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is wise to address the foundation before the furniture. However, let us remember that the most elegant system is one that requires the least effort to sustain. We must avoid creating a chore for ourselves.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"But if we spend the money on the screen and table, we won't have to pay for those outside rooms anymore! That's like saving money while getting a cool new toy! Isn't that the best way?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, you're totally right! Saving money and getting a better room is a win-win. But please, let's make sure it's a place where we can actually be honest and talk through things together!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm still not convinced that a fancy fit-out solves the ""who cleans up"" problem. If we're spending money, let's make sure we also agree on a fair usage schedule so it doesn't just become a lounge for two people!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"A schedule is a good idea, but it's secondary. If the room remains a place where every conversation is overheard by the office, people will continue to avoid it or seek outside rentals. Soundproofing is the priority.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Servas,,"We are circling the truth. If we invest in a space that truly serves us, the desire to maintain it will grow naturally. Let us choose the path that brings us together without adding burdens.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I think we should go for the screen and table! It stops us from wasting money on those outside rooms and makes it a place for everyone to gather. Let's make it a super-duper meeting spot!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with Sakura! If we get the screen and table, we can stop paying for outside rooms and finally have a place to talk properly. Let's make it a space where we can actually be friends!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
